# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VitaSDK
#
# ~494 MB of compiler, headers, stubs and host tools. Every clone installs its
# own copy, and nothing here builds without VITASDK set. Never commit it: it is
# a toolchain, not source, and it carries Sony-derived headers and stubs.
vitasdk/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
#
# Each project compiles into build/ and regenerates it from scratch. The
# BUILD_NUMBER file deliberately lives outside build/ (see AGENTS.md): wiping
# the build directory must not reuse a number that is already on the console.
build/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake

# Vita artifacts, wherever they land
*.vpk
*.vpk.out
*.velf
*.self
*.self.out
*.skprx
*.suprx
*.elf
*.a

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Console data
#
# A .psp2dmp is a full copy of the console's process memory, including mapped
# system modules. It is analysis input, not source, and must not be published.
*.psp2dmp
*.psp2dmp.tmp
*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party tools
#
# psp2_gpucrash_parse is shoui520's MIT project with its own history and
# license. Clone it into tools/ when you need it; do not vendor it. See
# gpu-crash-study/ANALYSIS.md.
tools/psp2_gpucrash_parse/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host tooling
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local console data
#
# A real config.txt kept as a parser fixture. The app must never ship one, and
# the tests build their own synthetic configs, so it stays out of the repo.
user-files/
